
# @summary The openpgp record that signs what this database exports -- and the signer a receiver expects
# Empty by default and required by export, import and restore. One attest
# identity per database: the dump and the bundle's MANIFEST are signed with
# it, and on the receiving side the SAME setting names the record whose
# fingerprint an incoming dump and MANIFEST must carry (pinned; expired,
# revoked or foreign keys are refused). Pinning is the trust decision, made
# once and explicitly -- a fresh database imports nothing until its owner
# has registered the sender's key and named it here.
#   elebake openpgp add manifest-attest 4E1F0A2B7C9D8E6F5A4B3C2D1E0F9A8B7C6D5E4F
#   elebake setenv ELEBAKE_ARCHIVE_ATTEST_KEY manifest-attest
# @see ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_attest
